  "projects": [
   {
    "title": "Don't Throw Me Away",
    "description": "From our project leader\nDon’t Throw Me Away is a platforming game about flow and cooperation. The game emphasizes cooperation by balancing game mastery and difficulty to create a unique play experience. Two players will take control of simple geometric avatars that are linked together. Together, players journey through a minimalist and abstract world that will test their individual skill and teamwork. Each level of the game world will have a series of floating nodes that the players must string together. Activating all the nodes in a level allows players to progress through the game. In order to restore reach these nodes, players must utilize the dynamics of being tethered to one another. This bond will provide a framework for the movement system of the game. Players must tug, throw or swing each other to traverse the level. The level design of the game will reinforce the movement system by focusing on the bond the two players share and their discovery of the abstract world. Don’t Throw Me Away aims to explore methods of generating flow in a cooperative space. ",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2016 - Present"
   },
   {
    "title": "Stealth Invasion! Crimea",
    "description": "Stealth Invasion! Crimea is a stealth based game inspired by the invasion of Crimea in 2014, and made a light-hearted take on the situation. The player takes control of soldiers and tries to hide them in the city without being spotted. The game was developed in JavaScript by a group of four students",
    "dateRange": {},
    "associatedWith": "Jan 2015 - Present"
